      "category": "process",
      "severity": "critical",
      "description": "The operating point crosses the stall line (system resistance too high, damper or blade pitch too closed, or two parallel fans unevenly loaded). Rotating stall cells form, giving sub-synchronous pulsation and blade stress; in a large system this can grow into surge with flow reversal.",
      "typical_progression": "Seconds. Sustained stall can fatigue blades within hours.",
      "required_roles": [
        "differential_pressure"
